{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery","id":1406873,"title":"What breaks if you shrink the tiers of sorcery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-07T18:38:08-07:00","id":1406873,"title":"What breaks if you shrink the tiers of sorcery?","content":"So in all the versions of Exalted, there are 3 tiers of sorcery. <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded and mortals get Emerald. Lunars/ Sidereals get Celestial. Solars get Adamant. <br /> <br /> Kinda like martial arts, only that you can't punch through tiers. <br /> <br /> What if there are charms that let you get higher? Dragonblooded, at Essence 4/5, can start trying to learn celestial circle sorcery. There's an extra surcharge of xp, but its possible. Lunars and Sidereals get to use Solar circle sorcery if they hit essence 5/6. Solars remain unchanged. <br /> <br /> Presume this for either 2e or 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:00:00-07:00","id":1406875,"title":"","content":"What breaks? Mostly just the entire setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:35:06-07:00","id":1406882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406875#post1406875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks? Mostly just the entire setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Unbalances the different types of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T20:01:34-07:00","id":1406889,"title":"","content":"Hmm well its limited to the movers and shakers and elders so its not like it would be common. I am curious and the pros and cons. Certainly with Solar Sorcery being available that is such a huge change, but well adding Sorcerous Workings kind of already did that. And the Protocols of Autochthonia already just divide things into two levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T20:01:36-07:00","id":1406890,"title":"","content":"The return of the Solars becomes one degree less of a Big Deal.<br /> <br /> (The <b>prospect</b> that the newly-returned Solars will eventually be capable of whistling up Third Circle Demons to do their bidding again has got various characters in my Lunars game <i>very tense</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T20:32:54-07:00","id":1406892,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406875#post1406875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What breaks? Mostly just the entire setting.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is an assertion that could use with citing the capabilities of Celestial Circle Sorcery that are setting breaking in the hands of a few dozen extra Exalted than the ones that are already capable of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heck, the assumption that there are even a few dozen Essence 4 or 5 Terrestrial Exalted is probably a bit generous, but say we are feeling charitable. What are they contributing that is setting breaking?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406890#post1406890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (The <b>prospect</b> that the newly-returned Solars will eventually be capable of whistling up Third Circle Demons to do their bidding again has got various characters in my Lunars game <i>very tense</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a very casual way of rendering something that can only be attempted once per year and only during a five day window of each year.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking, it's narrower even than that. If the ritual doesn't begin at sundown then it has to wait until tomorrow. We're not really given a clear indication on how Ritual spells might have their casting sufficiently interrupted to reset the clock for the caster, but presumably it is a consideration, and one even more severe for the demon-summoning spells considering their strict time slots.<br /> <br /> (I'm presuming that the same sorcerer can't summon a new demon each night of Calibration based on the description of the Second Circle spell).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T20:49:20-07:00","id":1406894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406892#post1406892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is an assertion that could use with citing the capabilities of Celestial Circle Sorcery that are setting breaking in the hands of a few dozen extra Exalted than the ones that are already capable of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heck, the assumption that there are even a few dozen Essence 4 or 5 Terrestrial Exalted is probably a bit generous, but say we are feeling charitable. What are they contributing that is setting breaking?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the kinda the idea. You want to cast celestial circle sorcery? Cool. Hit Essence 5. That's no big deal. Let's not forget that most Dragonblooded don't get past Essence 3. If you've hit Essence 5, and *also* gotten Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery? <br /> <br /> Fuck it, ok. Then you can get to summon Octavian (If he breaks loose hope you've got a brotherhood on standby). It's something you've pretty much earned. It means that you're the equivalent of that grandmaster with access to Celestial martial arts, fighting and crushing entire solar circles with his trusty white jade goremaul. <br /> <br /> You're the big boss. You're the guy that sits at the very top of the heap. Skipping one extra step of sorcery isn't that insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T21:53:44-07:00","id":1406901,"title":"","content":"There's one other thing to consider: Is this the rule or the exception.<br /> <br /> If <b>The Dragon-Blooded</b> can learn higher tier sorcery it breaks down the barrier between the exalted tiers, which is less important at the table (Where meaningful player contribution and impressive legendary challenges are what matter), but more important for the status quo of the setting, the less of a disparity there is between the Terrestrial and Celestial Exalted, the less significant the threat of the Silver Pact or the returned Solars is to the Realm. DB's outnumber the other exalted put together by about 20/1, so greater feats of prowess are needed to be able to combat the lands under their control, after all, unlike a Lunar cult leader or Solar chosen king, the DB can be practically everywhere at once.<br /> <br /> If <i>this Dragon-Blooded </i>can learn higher tiers of sorcery nothing breaks and it becomes a cool way of building up a player or introducing a new threat. Much like how celestial-level exigents in 3e present credible threats of great power, but being unique their threat to the status-quo is localized. Creation at your table is the place your game is taking place in, and that can be as small as a single city whose legacy was shaped by an exigent that is fundamental to your game, but to Creation as a whole, the Exigents contributed less because they've always acted as individuals rather than a longstanding faction. A single dragon-blood who learns higher tiers of sorcery will be considered a champion of their house, and a credible threat to the Anathema scourge, that makes them uniquely suited to whatever game is being run (either as a pro or antagonist) since they stand out from their fellows.<br /> <br /> In Essence that's one of the things they're apparently aiming for; artifacts and secret techniques that can heighten the power of individual exalted (such as the Mantle of Brighid) to better enable mixed play, without changing the overall status quo of creation. In short it's better to keep these as exceptions that apply to characters in <i>this particular </i>game, rather than the entirety of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 08-10-2020, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T21:58:19-07:00","id":1406902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406901#post1406901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one other thing to consider: Is this the rule or the exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of an exception is a Dragonblooded hitting Essence 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T22:10:34-07:00","id":1406903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406902#post1406902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of an exception is a Dragonblooded hitting Essence 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to you, the exact statistics are up to the storyteller, and at the table will appear in groups proportional to their importance (i.e. The capital of the realm likely has several on standby in case of a major crisis).<br /> Consider again though that <i>just </i>Essence 5 is only the first prerequisite, perhaps the means through which a Dragon-Blooded can learn these techniques are known only to either Bronze Faction Sidereal Masters or to ancient ghosts of the first age. Now it's not enough to <i>just </i>have this power, you have to be capable of finding this knowledge. Sidereals are cagey with their knowledge and unlikely to let you live if they share their techniques, and going to the underworld means you may well need to get past a Deathlord to accomplish this, but if you do perhaps you <i>can </i>teach this technique and now the realm's greatest champions have a brand new weapon against the resurgent Solars that you worked hard to get, or makes a surefire defeat of the realm at the Circle's hands suddenly look to be far more questionable.<br /> <br /> Can it happen? Sure. But it should be an exception or a change in the status quo, something that's a real game-changer. There have been high essence dragon-blooded since forever and none of them did it on their own. Now this one can? I smell a plot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 08-08-2020, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T22:51:59-07:00","id":1406905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406894#post1406894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the kinda the idea. You want to cast celestial circle sorcery? Cool. Hit Essence 5. That's no big deal. Let's not forget that most Dragonblooded don't get past Essence 3. If you've hit Essence 5, and *also* gotten Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery?<br /> <br /> Fuck it, ok. Then you can get to summon Octavian (If he breaks loose hope you've got a brotherhood on standby). It's something you've pretty much earned. It means that you're the equivalent of that grandmaster with access to Celestial martial arts, fighting and crushing entire solar circles with his trusty white jade goremaul.<br /> <br /> You're the big boss. You're the guy that sits at the very top of the heap. Skipping one extra step of sorcery isn't that insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, part of the reason they don't is that the time spent meditating under a water fall is something a lot of them consider a pain in the ass not worth undergoing to get essence 4-5 stuff. Essence 3 already gives dragon blooded a really big chunk of their really great charms compared to how many you get at 4 or 5, after all. Make it so that getting to a higher essence does give an extremely tangible benefit in letting you access sapphire circle goodies and that is going to be a change to the effort vs benefit ratio for sorcerer type dragon blooded. So more are going to push for essence 5 to get sapphire workings and summon Octavian once they get there instead of settling at a comfortable 3. Sure that is still probably not going to be a big percentage of them, but it doesn't have to be to upset the power balance given how many dragon blooded there are compared to other exalts. It would probably be enough to equal the number of lunars who are inclined to learn sorcerery and have reached essence 3+ to be able to initiate into 2nd circle and there goes one of the advantages lunars have over the dragon blooded. Especially since a good part of the strategy of the silver pact is breaking shit that the dragon blooded can't easily repair because they can't do high level workings or craft well compared to the exalts who made the now broken things. Having sapphire working capable dragon blooded running around makes places like Lookshy and the Realm more capable of maintaining and repairing the ancient wonders of the first age. So even though lunars get 3rd circle if they get to 5 that would still leave them with dragon blooded being better at keeping things going and hurt their strategy.<br /> <br /> Edit: And then it also takes away from the solars if they declare they are going to master the arcane secrets of the 3rd circle that has been gone from Creation for thousands of years only for someone to reply 'What are you talking about? Raksi has been doing 3rd circle sorceress stuff for nearly 2 millennia now and turned Mahalanka into a glorious kingdom of magical wonder! Though I guess she could always use an apprentice to help her keep it up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-08-2020, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T01:04:10-07:00","id":1406918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406905#post1406905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And then it also takes away from the solars if they declare they are going to master the arcane secrets of the 3rd circle that has been gone from Creation for thousands of years only for someone to reply 'What are you talking about? Raksi has been doing 3rd circle sorceress stuff for nearly 2 millennia now and turned Mahalanka into a glorious kingdom of magical wonder! Though I guess she could always use an apprentice to help her keep it up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't believe I'm saying this, but.... <br /> <br /> That's ok. <br /> <br /> Solars already have access to the strongest charms and most powerful dice adders. Patronage of the most powerful gods, as well as being the 'main character' splat. Losing Solar sorcery to other Lunars isn't something that I would count as bad. I think there's nothing wrong with giving the others guy's something more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T02:06:38-07:00","id":1406922,"title":"","content":"Genuine question: What's your preferred definition of &quot;breaks&quot;?<br /> <br /> I don't think the setting becomes untenable in the sense of the basic facts of the setting becoming untenable at all; the Dragon-Blooded can still hold the Realm, the Solars can still be usurped, the world can still be an Age of Sorrows that has lost much First Age glory etc. Esp. if you're willing to flex other things around to compensate.<br /> <br /> But if you want the &quot;feel&quot; of Solar sorcery being a lost power, Celestial sorcery being an dread power out of reach for Dragon-Blooded - of course that is not going to be quite the same!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T04:04:50-07:00","id":1406937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery#post1406873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in all the versions of Exalted, there are 3 tiers of sorcery.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded and mortals get Emerald. Lunars/ Sidereals get Celestial. Solars get Adamant.<br /> <br /> Kinda like martial arts, only that you can't punch through tiers.<br /> <br /> What if there are charms that let you get higher? Dragonblooded, at Essence 4/5, can start trying to learn celestial circle sorcery. There's an extra surcharge of xp, but its possible. Lunars and Sidereals get to use Solar circle sorcery if they hit essence 5/6. Solars remain unchanged.<br /> <br /> Presume this for either 2e or 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your best approach at shrinking the tiers of sorcery is removing the adamant circle entirely. That tier is more or less the solars' exclusive playground, and you can make a more sensical variation of sorcery on your terms by removing it entirely and giving solars something else for their sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T04:22:28-07:00","id":1406941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406937#post1406937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your best approach at shrinking the tiers of sorcery is removing the adamant circle entirely. That tier is more or less the solars' exclusive playground, and you can make a more sensical variation of sorcery on your terms by removing it entirely and giving solars something else for their sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what? <br /> <br /> Making an even bigger circle, called primordial circle sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T04:41:59-07:00","id":1406943,"title":"","content":"Can't they already do this just with the &quot;going beyong&quot;rules ? It's only for working but for the purpose of summoning or making big changes it doesn't really change anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 08-08-2020, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T04:46:59-07:00","id":1406946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406941#post1406941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?<br /> <br /> Making an even bigger circle, called primordial circle sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. And for all effects adamant tier is already that as far as anyone cares.<br /> <br /> I said remove the tier entirely, not add a new one.<br /> <br /> So you'd only have emerald and sapphire, and almost nothing of adamant would go down into sapphire. The tier would simply be gone, sorcery just won't do that anymore. Give the solar a handful of charms to cast harder and work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-08-2020, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T05:50:19-07:00","id":1406954,"title":"","content":"I think the war between the Sids and the Pact would look a lot different if the leadership on both sides could call half a dozen 3rd Circle Demons to their aid. In that Scenario, either one side has already won, or there's a whole lot more devastation and chaos throughout Creation overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-08-2020, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T06:39:44-07:00","id":1406957,"title":"","content":"If the empress still had the mantle of brigid that would mean she'd have access to solar circle. <br /> <br /> That's gonna have repercussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:01:54-07:00","id":1406958,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406943#post1406943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't they already do this just with the &quot;going beyong&quot;rules ?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Such a product does not exist sir. I think you must have dreamed it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> (Okay, I actually did miss the fact that you were referring specifically to workings as well, but I love that quote too much to be willing to delete it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406954#post1406954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the war between the Sids and the Pact would look a lot different if the leadership on both sides could call half a dozen 3rd Circle Demons to their aid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which demons do you have in mind?<br /> <br /> Let's also think about logistics here. Where exactly are you summoning them? How fast are they? How <i>stealthy</i> are they? Is the six hour ritual for summoning Third Circle Demons the kind of thing that might carry any kind of signifiers to mortal or Essence sight that may alert others if you try doing it closer to your target (and hence closer to the people that might arrive and try to interrupt you and render your work for naught).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that Scenario, either one side has already won, or there's a whole lot more devastation and chaos throughout Creation overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is not called &quot;Third Circle Demon&quot; and they're only unquestionable in Hell.<br /> <br /> I mean, do you presume that the monsters that Raksi raised against the Shogunate were axiomatically inferior to those demons? She's capable of Solar Circle Workings, it may be within her power to create her own entities of equivalent power outright.<br /> <br /> When such things are directed against the Realm, that might be the level of escalation that prompts the response of warstriders, Sidereals riding lesser elemental dragons while leading a battalion of the Aerial Legion, and the Sword of Creation itself to intercept it.<br /> <br /> As for the capacity for the Shogunate/Realm and Sidereals to turn their own examples of such power back upon the Silver Pact? Sure they probably have some advantages. The thing that has been the state of the world throughout the Second Age. The Silver Pact retains its tools of evasion and seclusion and versatility, of insinuation and sabotage.<br /> <br /> Still, in a world where Sidereals and Lunars could summon and bind Third Circle Demons, is one presuming that they would do so without reservation? Is this also a version of the setting where there never was the tradition of the Calibration Feast, the long-standing setting signifier of &quot;even the Solars at the height of the Old Realm had reservations against the summoning of Third Circle Demons&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a thing that would cause chaos and devastation throughout Creation, and hence would be something that people who need to live there would be super juiced about doing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just like our world, in which nuclear weapons were invented and then used constantly. Nobody in severe hostility with one another ever thought it was sensible to maybe keep them in reserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:21:45-07:00","id":1406961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406958#post1406958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Such a product does not exist sir. I think you must have dreamed it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> (Okay, I actually did miss the fact that you were referring specifically to workings as well, but I love that quote too much to be willing to delete it.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I dont know the reference could you explain it to me ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T08:26:16-07:00","id":1406975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406902#post1406902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of an exception is a Dragonblooded hitting Essence 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rare, but I also think there's something to be said about soemthing rare in a &quot;There aren't many DBs, so the Charm is contrained&quot; sense, and rare in the &quot;You having access to this is outside the nroms&quot; sense. There's something different about an artifact ala Mantle of Brigid or the Emerald Thurible giving Dragon-Blooded access to higher sorcery effects versus it being an assumed default only constrained by raw power. One is a side-effect of just being Essence 5, the other is an actual exception beyond that.<br /> <br /> Basically in this context, I think it's fine so long as it's an exception. But in that context, it's probably not just some Essence 5 Occult Charm speedbump but probably an artifact, or some other great unique project that allowed for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:06:22-07:00","id":1406981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406958#post1406958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which demons do you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having joined during 3e I don't know 3rd Circles well, I'm just going from the idea that they were dangerous enough that Calibration feasts were a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406958#post1406958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, in a world where Sidereals and Lunars could summon and bind Third Circle Demons, is one presuming that they would do so without reservation? Is this also a version of the setting where there never was the tradition of the Calibration Feast, the long-standing setting signifier of &quot;even the Solars at the height of the Old Realm had reservations against the summoning of Third Circle Demons&quot;?<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a thing that would cause chaos and devastation throughout Creation, and hence would be something that people who need to live there would be super juiced about doing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just like our world, in which nuclear weapons were invented and then used constantly. Nobody in severe hostility with one another ever thought it was sensible to maybe keep them in reserve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our world isn't ruled by magic people cursed to give in to their worst impulses on a regular basis, so I would draw a distinction there.<br /> <br /> Also the choice of Sids to use the calibration feast as an opportunity to kill all other Celestials might very well have convinced more than a few Lunars to throw out anything to do with the feasts, including the wisdom behind them. Sure, it's not a rational thought, but it's a very human one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-08-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:34:55-07:00","id":1407032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406905#post1406905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind, part of the reason they don't is that the time spent meditating under a water fall is something a lot of them consider a pain in the ass not worth undergoing to get essence 4-5 stuff. Essence 3 already gives dragon blooded a really big chunk of their really great charms compared to how many you get at 4 or 5, after all. Make it so that getting to a higher essence does give an extremely tangible benefit in letting you access sapphire circle goodies and that is going to be a change to the effort vs benefit ratio for sorcerer type dragon blooded. So more are going to push for essence 5 to get sapphire workings and summon Octavian once they get there instead of settling at a comfortable 3. Sure that is still probably not going to be a big percentage of them, but it doesn't have to be to upset the power balance given how many dragon blooded there are compared to other exalts. It would probably be enough to equal the number of lunars who are inclined to learn sorcerery and have reached essence 3+ to be able to initiate into 2nd circle and there goes one of the advantages lunars have over the dragon blooded. Especially since a good part of the strategy of the silver pact is breaking shit that the dragon blooded can't easily repair because they can't do high level workings or craft well compared to the exalts who made the now broken things. Having sapphire working capable dragon blooded running around makes places like Lookshy and the Realm more capable of maintaining and repairing the ancient wonders of the first age. So even though lunars get 3rd circle if they get to 5 that would still leave them with dragon blooded being better at keeping things going and hurt their strategy.<br /> <br /> Edit: And then it also takes away from the solars if they declare they are going to master the arcane secrets of the 3rd circle that has been gone from Creation for thousands of years only for someone to reply 'What are you talking about? Raksi has been doing 3rd circle sorceress stuff for nearly 2 millennia now and turned Mahalanka into a glorious kingdom of magical wonder! Though I guess she could always use an apprentice to help her keep it up.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with your Edit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T17:16:27-07:00","id":1407051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406961#post1406961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm sorry I dont know the reference could you explain it to me ? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You don't watch The Simpsons? Damn, that's unfortunate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Although if you watch it dubbed to your own language, perhaps that's a joke that was worded differently.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406981#post1406981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having joined during 3e I don't know 3rd Circles well, I'm just going from the idea that they were dangerous enough that Calibration feasts were a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a perilous quality to them, but they're not nuclear weapons.<br /> <br /> Heck, of the original five introduced, two of them are primarily based on infrastructure; the voice of Jacint lays great roads that can go anywhere, and Orabilis raises grand glass libraries filled with significant lore (although delving too deep may bring you to secrets that only the Yozis may know, at which point he shall become obligated to lay hands on you and cast you into the skies of Hell, there to wither under the pitiless light of Ligier and be reduced to one of their bleak stars).<br /> <br /> Even Ligier, the most overtly martial of them, is first and foremost a peerless smith (who in his kindness would make Creation as Malfeas is, to share in its poisonous beauty). He prostrates himself before princes and pauper smiths to offer his services, and his pride is such that he will not deliberately make anything flawed (although it is impossible for him to not include flaws in a work that does not include some manner of willingly offered sacrifice).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our world isn't ruled by magic people cursed to give in to their worst impulses on a regular basis, so I would draw a distinction there.</div> </div> </div> </div>But their policies still manage to be governed by a form of reason often enough.<br /> <br /> (Notwithstanding that even for the Monstrous Urge of Lunars, &quot;worst impulses&quot; is a tad one-sided.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the choice of Sids to use the calibration feast as an opportunity to kill all other Celestials might very well have convinced more than a few Lunars to throw out anything to do with the feasts, including the wisdom behind them. Sure, it's not a rational thought, but it's a very human one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it could.<br /> <br /> But if somebody was proposing a house rule in which it was possible for Lunars to summon and bind Third Circle Demons, and a person perceives that as the kind of thing that could lay waste to the world if not done with restraint, it probably shouldn't be. I mean, unless they find the premise of playing in the aftermath of the ruined world compelling, which sure it can be. But everything is in place to act as though characters still treat it as perilous so that the house rule has a world to play in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T19:10:44-07:00","id":1407065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406961#post1406961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I dont know the reference could you explain it to me ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an episode of <i>The Simpsons</i> in which Homer comes to Apu's shop feeling kinda down, so he asks Apu for &quot;Skittlebrau,&quot; a beer with candy floating in it. Apu's reply is what Isator said, so Homer resigns himself to buying beer and Skittles and doing it himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T21:08:11-07:00","id":1407074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406943#post1406943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't they already do this just with the &amp;quot;going beyong&amp;quot;rules ? It's only for working but for the purpose of summoning or making big changes it doesn't really change anything</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Circle Sorcery is the difference between taking a month vs. a year to perform a Celestial working and six to eight years vs. one for a Solar working. Times that by the thousand years DBs have been in charge and you get a very different Second Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T01:24:28-07:00","id":1407103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407074#post1407074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celestial Circle Sorcery is the difference between taking a month vs. a year to perform a Celestial working and six to eight years vs. one for a Solar working. Times that by the thousand years DBs have been in charge and you get a very different Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure what's your point. I mean they already can do that, and the fact that it takes them a year to do a Celestial working (or even 5 years) wouldn't change anything I think. When you are trying to make changes on the scale of Celestial workings I don't think few years is a project blocker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T05:36:33-07:00","id":1407123,"title":"","content":"Simply declaring that all exalts have access to sorcery of a higher tier would break the setting. If DBs had access to celestial circle, and Lunars/Sids could use solar all along, history of the setting would be vastly different.<br /> <br /> BUT, if you made this improved access a new thing, it could work. Blame it all on the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade. The vast alien energies that flooded Creation had a greater effect on the essence of the world than anyone could have imagined. Add in the heavy use of the Sword of Creation/Realm Defense Grid. It was never tested for such a heavy use, and was in poor maintenance. Who knows what long term effects it caused? So now, a few hundred years after those events, a tiny number of Exalted are discovering ability for sorcery that goes against the facts that everyone knows. (This isn't to say that only a tiny number can access stronger magic, but only a tiny number will stumble upon the ability.)<br /> <br /> Gaining a higher than normal initiation would be very difficult, but not impossible. Those who discover the ability would certainly keep it to themselves. Having that sort of power would paint a target on anyone's back. Also, getting access to higher spells would be difficult in the extreme. So the newly minted Celestial and Solar sorcerers would have to invent their own spells from scratch. Let's take Raksi as an example. Maybe she broke into Solar tier centuries ago. But She's so obsessed with getting the spells from the Book of 3 Circles that she's never even considered trying to create her own Solar Circle spells.<br /> <br /> Solars will still have an advantage over other sorcerers. Solars are innately capable of all circles of sorcery. They can gain initiation intuitively, and can practice their magic with no more risk than they already have by simply being Solars. Same goes with DBs vs Sids/Lunars in the realm of Celestial Circle sorcery. If you include necromancy too, Abysals will still have the immense advantage of Deathlords teaching them the darkest secrets of Labyrinth Circle necromancy vs. everyone else stumbling along blindly.<br /> <br /> Approaching access to higher tier sorcery this way will allow a storyteller to make a few antagonists who have extra power, and allow players to get unusual advantages without breaking the setting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/472-keldorn2198","name":"Keldorn2198","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T06:47:55-07:00","id":1407132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1406943#post1406943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't they already do this just with the &quot;going beyong&quot;rules ? It's only for working but for the purpose of summoning or making big changes it doesn't really change anything</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, a sorcerer CAN attempt a working to alter itself in such a way that might allow for them to access a circle above their capacities (among other things), i would guess.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Create a loyal minion with supernatural powers comparable to a Second Circle demon or notable god</i>&quot;, ergo, someone like Mara who's versed in the Sapphire Circle, <b>is an Ambition 3 Celestial Circle Working</b>, according to the book itself. I would guess that remaking oneself in such a being might count as the same, so there's a good ballpark for insanely ambitious/foolhardy Dragon-Blooded (<b><i>or mortals</i></b>) to strive for.<br /> <br /> Trying the same for Adamant Circle <i>might</i> count as &quot;<i>Create a supernatural being of a singular nature and considerable power</i>&quot;, <b>an Ambition 3 Celestial Circle Working</b>, depending on an individual ST's personal preference/interpretation of the &quot;<i>singular nature and considerable power</i>&quot; part. Good luck with pulling that off, for those brave enough to try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As long as it is a dramatic and risky undertaking to occur ingame, for PCs to attempt - or sabotage their enemies' efforts - instead of a charm-based XP tax to stamp upon, i guess i'm pretty ok with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-09-2020, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T16:47:35-07:00","id":1407200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407074#post1407074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celestial Circle Sorcery is the difference between taking a month vs. a year to perform a Celestial working and six to eight years vs. one for a Solar working. Times that by the thousand years DBs have been in charge and you get a very different Second Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many Essence 5 Dragon Blooded do you suppose there are in the Realm?<br /> <br /> How many of those would you say are sorcerers? Sure, we have Mnemon, Berit, probably Ragara. Any more?<br /> <br /> I'll note that of those, Mnemon has many responsibilities that take up her attention to a degree that I imagine she can't even put together as many Terrestrial Workings as are within her capabilities. Fair enough that Mnemon's work ethic is probably unique even among House founders, but still, an Essence 5 Dragon Blood might be expected to have a lot of things to focus on that mean that they can't send off these hypothetical Celestial Workings with complete impunity.<br /> <br /> So sure, a <i>slightly</i> different Second Age. But perhaps not quite that different.<br /> <br /> Mind, a question is raised of whether or not the Great Houses on the whole have the same attitudes with regards to sorcery. With enough time, this legendary potentate might be able to make their home prefecture as grand as Raksi's domain, but might that not disturb their neighbours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:20:42-07:00","id":1407203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407200#post1407200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many Essence 5 Dragon Blooded do you suppose there are in the Realm?<br /> <br /> How many of those would you say are sorcerers? Sure, we have Mnemon, Berit, probably Ragara. Any more?<br /> <br /> I'll note that of those, Mnemon has many responsibilities that take up her attention to a degree that I imagine she can't even put together as many Terrestrial Workings as are within her capabilities. Fair enough that Mnemon's work ethic is probably unique even among House founders, but still, an Essence 5 Dragon Blood might be expected to have a lot of things to focus on that mean that they can't send off these hypothetical Celestial Workings with complete impunity.<br /> <br /> So sure, a <i>slightly</i> different Second Age. But perhaps not quite that different.<br /> <br /> Mind, a question is raised of whether or not the Great Houses on the whole have the same attitudes with regards to sorcery. With enough time, this legendary potentate might be able to make their home prefecture as grand as Raksi's domain, but might that not disturb their neighbours?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cathak Cainan is, per What Fire Has Wrought, as are Cevis Ghandavra (though not of the Realm, he's helpful for knowing what an essence 5 db can look like) and Ragara per Heirs of the Shogunate. Amon Mora, Tepet Arada, Peleps Deled and Cathak Setod are essence 4.<br /> <br /> That makes me think it likely that at least a few other heads of houses are essence 5, as well as probably some people associated with the Immaculate Order. My guess would be 10-100 dragonblooded of essence 5 in the Realm, but I don't think we're given a lot to go on.<br /> <br /> Assuming 100 dynasts exalt each year (average lifespan ~100, there are 10,000 dynasts), and since a few dozen are enrolled in the Heptagram at a time, they enroll for 7 years, and some don't graduate, probably something like 2-10% of Dynasts graduated from the Heptagram. Add in various who become sorcerers from another source, and you have probably around 10% of dynasts are sorcerers. (Compare to 20% of dynasts have occult as a caste ability, and if all abilities are favored at an equal rate 20% have occult as a favored ability. Assuming we should treat caste/favored as anything other than game mechanics, I'd expect nearly all sorcerers to have occult as caste/favored, and many people with occult caste/favored not to be sorcerers). For comparison, 20% of the known essence 5 dragonblooded are sorcerers, but 5 people is really not enough sample size for this.<br /> <br /> Assuming no correlation between these, I'm estimating 1-10 essence 5 dragonblooded dynasts are sorcerers. Plus maybe a few more outside the Realm.<br /> <br /> Though, it has been mentioned that part of the explanation of why there aren't many essence 5 dragonblooded is &quot;Why bother, essence 3 is strong enough&quot;, and if it's known that sufficient enlightenment allows sorcerers to reach dramatic new heights it might encourage more of them to seek that out.<br /> <br /> Given how rough nearly all of these numbers are, it seems reasonable for the final result to be fairly different than I got (though, clearly at least 1, since Mnemon is an Essence 5 Sorcerer)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 08-09-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:46:44-07:00","id":1407206,"title":"","content":"It would also raise the capabilities of those that did get there. You can only use a working to pull off stuff one tier above your capability, so presently Dragonblood can't punch higher than Celestial tier. Now obviously this is nothing to sneeze at, but it does change things the Realm and the Shogunate before it if plans could be made to drag out the ravine of whispers as a territorial obstacle, and how many demons had lovely siege breaker abilities . Of course the balance is these things are then easily accessibly for the more sorcerously inclined Lunars, read Raksi for an obvious one, as they no longer need a working to get the same results on pulling some of the biggest monsters into the field.<br /> <br /> The setting probably risks becoming a cold war in that aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:48:11-07:00","id":1407207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407203#post1407203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cevis Ghandavra (though not of the Realm, he's helpful for knowing what an essence 5 db can look like)</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't read Heirs of the Shogunate until it is released properly, but I would expect that between the Sea of Mind and whatever the name of the Artifact that allows him to continuously reincarnate is called, he's not typical of anything at all about the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> I wonder if his current write-up obligates him to rebuild his Essence from scratch during each lifetime.<br /> <br /> (That's a question for myself, I don't want to know much of anything about the contents of Heirs until I read it firsthand)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes me think it likely that at least a few other heads of houses are essence 5</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps one of the Cynis sisters, maybe Ledaal Yasmet. Peleps Lai sounds like she has the correct age and stature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXauY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess would be 10-100 dragonblooded of essence 5 in the Realm, but I don't think we're given a lot to go on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an enormous leap from &quot;House heads and some venerable Immaculates&quot; to &quot;up to one hundred&quot;.<br /> <br /> We don't have <i>much</i> to go on, but what we do, seems more inclined to far fewer Essence 5 Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXauY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, it has been mentioned that part of the explanation of why there aren't many essence 5 dragonblooded is &quot;Why bother, essence 3 is strong enough&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's an accurate reading of what the person said, nor to the presentation in the books. Essence 4 is described as a likely (but not definite) level of refinement for those that have exceeded a mortal lifetime. &quot;Essence 5 is a mark of extreme prowess, vanishingly rare among the ranks of the comparatively short-lived Dragon-Blooded and noteworthy even among centuries-old elder Celestial Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXauY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it's known that sufficient enlightenment allows sorcerers to reach dramatic new heights it might encourage more of them to seek that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was how it worked then I would already expect the majority of Essence 5 Dragon Blooded Charms to sufficiently motivate people towards it. I expect Arada is just kicking himself for having not put in the time to be capable of wielding the Dragon Vortex Attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXauY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how rough nearly all of these numbers are, it seems reasonable for the final result to be fairly different than I got (though, clearly at least 1, since Mnemon is an Essence 5 Sorcerer)</div> </div> </div> </div>Two, Berit is as well.<br /> <br /> She's also a weird recluse, per her bitterness over not being granted a remit to found a House and estrangement from her mother. The same character with more power might make only for a more unusual hermitage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T20:59:21-07:00","id":1407228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407103#post1407103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what's your point. I mean they already can do that, and the fact that it takes them a year to do a Celestial working (or even 5 years) wouldn't change anything I think. When you are trying to make changes on the scale of Celestial workings I don't think few years is a project blocker.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they could do dozens of Celestial workings in those few years instead of one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407200#post1407200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note that of those, Mnemon has many responsibilities that take up her attention to a degree that I imagine she can't even put together as many Terrestrial Workings as are within her capabilities. Fair enough that Mnemon's work ethic is probably unique even among House founders, but still, an Essence 5 Dragon Blood might be expected to have a lot of things to focus on that mean that they can't send off these hypothetical Celestial Workings with complete impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the <i>more</i> reason why the same workings taking 10% of the time would be a paradigm shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T00:20:51-07:00","id":1407243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407228#post1407228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if they could do dozens of Celestial workings in those few years instead of one?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All the <i>more</i> reason why the same workings taking 10% of the time would be a paradigm shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are so much DB that I'd argue they can already do that if they want to, at that point it's just a matter of ST perception of the Realm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T02:29:57-07:00","id":1407253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407207#post1407207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was how it worked then I would already expect the majority of Essence 5 Dragon Blooded Charms to sufficiently motivate people towards it. I expect Arada is just kicking himself for having not put in the time to be capable of wielding the Dragon Vortex Attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that holds.<br /> <br /> Charms aren't real. Arada doesn't watch Cainain engulf a battlefield in flames and think &quot;I wish I had Essence 5&quot;. Arada bathes the battlefield in lightning (using Essence 3 Storm-Calling Strategos) and thinks &quot;It's good to be a Prince of the Earth&quot;.<br /> <br /> They don't think of it in character as &quot;Essence 3 is good enough&quot; any more than a playground bully tries to rank their fighting skill out of five IRL.<br /> <br /> But sorcery is a real and formalised thing. Just like the kid being bullied is motivated to study karate and become a black-belt, the formal structure of sorcery promotes exactly this kind of &quot;I wish I was Essence 5&quot; thinking in a way that the DB Charms <i>which don't actually exist in setting</i> do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T02:59:25-07:00","id":1407257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407253#post1407253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that holds.<br /> <br /> Charms aren't real. Arada doesn't watch Cainain engulf a battlefield in flames and think &quot;I wish I had Essence 5&quot;. Arada bathes the battlefield in lightning (using Essence 3 Storm-Calling Strategos) and thinks &quot;It's good to be a Prince of the Earth&quot;.<br /> <br /> They don't think of it in character as &quot;Essence 3 is good enough&quot; any more than a playground bully tries to rank their fighting skill out of five IRL.<br /> <br /> But sorcery is a real and formalised thing. Just like the kid being bullied is motivated to study karate and become a black-belt, the formal structure of sorcery promotes exactly this kind of &quot;I wish I was Essence 5&quot; thinking in a way that the DB Charms <i>which don't actually exist in setting</i> do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that doesn't really count. Sure, there's no such thing as Essence 5. But he can always look at the shit Essence 5 dragonblooded do, and think: &quot;I wish I was that awesome.&quot; and meditate under a waterfall or in a hurricane or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:16:11-07:00","id":1407265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407257#post1407257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that doesn't really count. Sure, there's no such thing as Essence 5. But he can always look at the shit Essence 5 dragonblooded do, and think: &amp;quot;I wish I was that awesome.&amp;quot; and meditate under a waterfall or in a hurricane or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you <i>can</i> look at an awesome street fighter and want to get good at fighting.<br /> <br /> But you're <i>more likely</i> to look at someone with formalized training and wish to go through a similiar, ranked process (as with becoming a black-belt).<br /> <br /> Everything you learn in college could be learned at home with the internet. People still go to college, and the people who go to college (usually) pursue more education than those who don't.<br /> <br /> Also, Charms are linked to Abilities as well as Essence. You can't just meditate under a waterfall then unleash As In the Beginning. You have to be a world class scholar as well. And if you can already lash a battlefield with lightning... what really motivates you to become a world class scholar?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty good at mathematics. In the abstract, I could read at home and become better at math, then leverage that to do awesome things -- like Terence Tao. But if there's structure and an immediate pay-off (complete the math course at community college and we'll give you $500 cash) then I'm far more likely to complete that math course.<br /> <br /> (And this is without considers whether Solar workings with Celestial Sorcery are strictly better than DB Charms. I'm just talking about structure and tangibles here.)<br /> <br /> Unless your argument is that all the DBs who could reach Essence 5 do, and those who fall short could never reach Essence 5 no matter how they were motivated, I don't see how adding additional incentive to reach Essence 5 wouldn't cause more Exalted to reach Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:50:00-07:00","id":1407271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407265#post1407265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you <i>can</i> look at an awesome street fighter and want to get good at fighting.<br /> <br /> But you're <i>more likely</i> to look at someone with formalized training and wish to go through a similiar, ranked process (as with becoming a black-belt).<br /> <br /> Everything you learn in college could be learned at home with the internet. People still go to college, and the people who go to college (usually) pursue more education than those who don't.<br /> <br /> Also, Charms are linked to Abilities as well as Essence. You can't just meditate under a waterfall then unleash As In the Beginning. You have to be a world class scholar as well. And if you can already lash a battlefield with lightning... what really motivates you to become a world class scholar?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty good at mathematics. In the abstract, I could read at home and become better at math, then leverage that to do awesome things -- like Terence Tao. But if there's structure and an immediate pay-off (complete the math course at community college and we'll give you $500 cash) then I'm far more likely to complete that math course.<br /> <br /> (And this is without considers whether Solar workings with Celestial Sorcery are strictly better than DB Charms. I'm just talking about structure and tangibles here.)<br /> <br /> Unless your argument is that all the DBs who could reach Essence 5 do, and those who fall short could never reach Essence 5 no matter how they were motivated, I don't see how adding additional incentive to reach Essence 5 wouldn't cause more Exalted to reach Essence 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? <br /> <br /> This started this by you saying that more people would hit Essence 5 because there's a payoff of celestial sorcery, and wouldn't do so otherwise because they wouldn't bother trying harder, because they're pretty satisfied with what they have (like storm calling strategos). <br /> <br /> But I'm saying that's wrong, because Storm Calling Strategos is Essence 3, and more and more power is gained by climbing the steps of essence 4-5. If people aren't bothered to climb the power to get essence 5 and the accompanying power.... why would they bother getting essence 5 and celestial sorcery? <br /> <br /> You're saying that there is structure and pay off. But isn't that the same for Essence and Essence 5 DB charms? Unless you're saying that fundamentally, there's a difference between E5 charms and Celestial scale sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T05:19:43-07:00","id":1407276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407271#post1407271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're saying that there is structure and pay off. But isn't that the same for Essence and Essence 5 DB charms? Unless you're saying that fundamentally, there's a difference between E5 charms and Celestial scale sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are saying there is a fundamental difference between e5 charms and Celestial scale sorcery. Charms are discrete game representations of continuous continuous setting elements - as you grow stronger you can influence the elements in larger ways, but the specific charms are (mostly) not things characters in setting would recognize. And so if you study and meditate and reach greater enlightenment, you can expect to have some new capabilities, but not any specific new ones. Levels are sorcery are a discrete game representation of a discrete setting element - characters in story can recognize the clear difference between Emerald and Sapphire Sorcery. If you study and meditate and initiate into a new circle, you get access to specifically the same spells as other Sapphire Circle Sorcerers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T08:15:13-07:00","id":1407297,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also how one of the metrics for assigning circles to workings is \u201cHow easily should even the best DB sorcerers be able to do this.\u201d Upgrading DBs to Celestial sorcerers kind of throws that off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T03:05:10-07:00","id":1407472,"title":"","content":"I would say that, besides Demon of the Third Circle, there is not much difference in Solar spells to make them so game-breaking. Really, the 3rd circle speels are good, but not that much. Workings are only harder to get, if they are solar, so that's a non-issue (*). <br /> <br /> And then, Demon of the 3rd circle could be game-breaking or not, depending on how they statted. They have never had stats (in any edition - mind you), so it is the game master's choice. Are they 'you win' entities? Are their stats just more inflated? How much? Are they one-trick poneys?<br /> <br /> Also, there would be a matter of economics for demons of the 3rd circle. How? Well, a demon cannot be invoked twice at the same time. This is no issue with demons of the first circle, they are races, and plentiful.<br /> <br /> This starts to be a problem with demons of the second circle. Suppose you want to invoke Octavian, the Living Tower. For him to be available, you will need to beat every other invoker that would want to get him, if he was not invoked already. And if he is invoked, no luck this time, better luck next month (**). That will be more of a problem if there are (hundreds?) of DBs invoking.<br /> <br /> This is much more of a case with demons of the Third Circle, who are not so numerous to begin with. In the setting as written, in the beginning, it will be easy for the solar to invoke any demon and say they are the 'first of the age', but then later the issue will raise its ugly head again. And worse, if it's a miss, better luck next year! If there would already dozens of celestials calling them, this would a fucking rat race! There would be rushes to be the first to end a ritual in the year and get first pick, and chances are big that in the end, you would choose poorly just to be beaten to it and get nothing (***). <br /> <br /> And then there is an OOC issue: there aren't that many demons statted. If demon summoning is more prevalent, the storyteller would need to create more demons. This is a lot of work for 2nd circle demons, that have their unique things going on. This is a huge problem for demons of the third circle, for which we have nothing on the subject of stats. <br /> <br /> * - Except Solar ambition 3, but who cares! Sure, they are creation-spanning, but oh so very subtle. Everybody wants to make exalted-lite supersoldiers.<br /> ** - Really, going for broke on Summoning Octavian is a newbie mistake. It is a cutthroat market and you just won't get him! You should go for Joxer, the Obscure One. <br /> ***- It would be much safer to go to the obscure ones, again. And there would not be that many obscure ones, with there being so few and existing a living culture of invoking them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:23:09-07:00","id":1407532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery#post1406873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in all the versions of Exalted, there are 3 tiers of sorcery.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded and mortals get Emerald. Lunars/ Sidereals get Celestial. Solars get Adamant.<br /> <br /> Kinda like martial arts, only that you can't punch through tiers.<br /> <br /> What if there are charms that let you get higher? Dragonblooded, at Essence 4/5, can start trying to learn celestial circle sorcery. There's an extra surcharge of xp, but its possible. Lunars and Sidereals get to use Solar circle sorcery if they hit essence 5/6. Solars remain unchanged.<br /> <br /> Presume this for either 2e or 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Main issue I see with the proposal is that it draws further attention to how a group of PCs (especially Dragon-Blooded) tends to be supermen among the supermen simply because the narrative is following them. At least if they go and find something like the Emerald Thurible or the Mantle of Brigid that kind of power level seems warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T10:59:17-07:00","id":1407555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407472#post1407472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, Demon of the 3rd circle could be game-breaking or not, depending on how they statted. They have never had stats (in any edition - mind you), so it is the game master's choice. Are they 'you win' entities? Are their stats just more inflated? How much? Are they one-trick poneys?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, they had Ahlat's statline.<br /> In 2E, several of them got stats (as dicepools and Charms rather than Attributes and Abilities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T01:45:11-07:00","id":1407669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406873-what-breaks-if-you-shrink-the-tiers-of-sorcery?p=1407555#post1407555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E, they had Ahlat's statline.<br /> In 2E, several of them got stats (as dicepools and Charms rather than Attributes and Abilities).</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st ed, that might be that they had similar stats to Ahlat (as in Word from Grabowski), but there was not even one statted example for them. <br /> <br /> In. 2nd ed., I even forgot about that they were 'statted' later in the edition. Mind you, the descriptions of their sample abilities were in many ways were better than the indecent charm dump style we had earlier in the edition for npcs, but they had incomplete descriptions with no combat stats. As if you were not supposed to fight them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}